  "definition": {
    "id": "ACT-GRAM",
    "revision": 6,
    "title": "Express different meanings of would",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-would-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Express different meanings of would",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "English would has different meanings: 想 for a wish, 愿意 for willingness, and 会 for a predicted hypothetical result. Choose by meaning.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "我想喝茶。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ xiǎng hē chá 。",
                "meaning": "I would like some tea.",
                "audio": "f3e7b950a5ebf54040a0e5f650962e37c80456d639d69ec0a6e66b50a03f7b7e"
              },
              {
                "text": "我愿意帮助你。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ yuànyì bāngzhù nǐ 。",
                "meaning": "I would be willing to help you.",
                "audio": "bf4e0dd4983ef6e71f69a978cc4fc302abd136e8fffd42b5724a2776f269c46e"
              },
              {
                "text": "如果下雨，我会在家。",
                "pinyin": "rúguǒ xiàyǔ ， wǒ huì zài jiā 。",
                "meaning": "If it rained, I would be at home.",
                "audio": "92db2f1877a093178b6f30ef73ff5f19d00e2669436158e20984df8ec8b5792e"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Words used in this pattern",
